stable-diffusion.cpp: the VAE's convolutions in their weights' own precision (bf16 for Qwen-Image 2.1's VAE), not f16.

Why: Qwen-Image 2.1's VAE decoder carries activations past half's range (65,504). stable-diffusion.cpp made every VAE
conv weight f16, so ggml_conv_2d's im2col was f16 too: those activations became inf, then NaN, and the picture's bytes
came out 255 - opaque white blocks a latent pixel wide in the alpha (and the colour) wherever the background should be
clear (leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp#2024). Upstream's fix is PR #2043 (CarlGao4, open as of 2026-11-12); this is its
core - the conv blocks keep a VAE weight's stored type and compute in it, an f32 weight goes through an f32 im2col -
without its new --vae-dtype option, so sd_ctx_params_t (and the bridge, image/sd/sd.cpp) keep their layout.

Applied to the tree at 2bb7294 (kernels/build.sh's SDCPP and SDLIB defaults):
  rsync -a --exclude /build <stable-diffusion.cpp>/ ~/nextcuda/src/sdcpp-alpha/
  cd ~/nextcuda/src/sdcpp-alpha && patch -p1 < <this file>
  cmake -S . -B ../sdcpp-alpha-build -DSD_CUDA=ON -DSD_BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES="86;120" \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && make -C ../sdcpp-alpha-build -j8 stable-diffusion

